cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SeamScope or its pilot evidence package, please cite this software record."
title: "SeamScope: A Minimal Cyber-Physical Testbed for Route-Relative Test Evidence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Billie"
    given-names: "David"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-9205-1391"
abstract: >-
  SeamScope is a minimal cyber-physical mobile testbed for examining what an
  automated test result is evidence of when a shared Appium scenario executes
  through either a software injection seam or a serial-controlled physical
  Bluetooth Low Energy route. The archived research artifact includes the
  source, frozen protocol, route-relative claim-assessment companion, and a
  sanitized pilot evidence package.
version: 1.0.0
